1
00:00:01,316 --> 00:00:03,446
Meet a ParyonUSD borrower.

2
00:00:03,446 --> 00:00:06,664
She locked BCH and borrowed dollars against it.

3
00:00:07,268 --> 00:00:11,958
If her loan drops below 110% collateral, it is liquidated,

4
00:00:11,958 --> 00:00:14,364
and she loses all of that BCH.

5
00:00:14,364 --> 00:00:16,259
Prices crash at 3am.

6
00:00:16,259 --> 00:00:18,730
Today her only defence is to be awake,

7
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:21,352
with spare BCH ready to add by hand.

8
00:00:21,906 --> 00:00:23,844
Backstop is a safety net.

9
00:00:23,844 --> 00:00:26,442
She sets aside a BCH reserve, once.

10
00:00:26,442 --> 00:00:31,537
If her loan nears liquidation, anyone can move part of that reserve into her loan.

11
00:00:31,537 --> 00:00:35,587
She signs nothing, and the contract makes sure that is all they can do.

12
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,794
Setup is one signature.

13
00:00:40,794 --> 00:00:43,501
She picks a reserve and sees what it buys her:

14
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:45,973
her loan can absorb a much deeper fall.

15
00:00:45,973 --> 00:00:51,836
A rescue starts below the level she chooses and lifts the loan back to 150%.

16
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:01,222
Could a keeper cheat?

17
00:01:01,222 --> 00:01:03,415
This one tries to copy her loan key.

18
00:01:03,415 --> 00:01:05,972
The contract refuses, and names the rule.

19
00:01:05,972 --> 00:01:08,550
Paryon's own contracts would have let it through.

20
00:01:09,458 --> 00:01:11,303
Now BCH crashes.

21
00:01:11,303 --> 00:01:13,901
Her loan falls to 115%.

22
00:01:13,901 --> 00:01:17,315
A keeper with no keys and no money sends the rescue.

23
00:01:17,315 --> 00:01:21,897
The reserve flows into her loan, and it is back near 150%.

24
00:01:21,897 --> 00:01:25,101
She was asleep.

25
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:33,383
And she can always leave.

26
00:01:33,383 --> 00:01:36,665
One signature returns her loan key and her reserve.

27
00:01:36,665 --> 00:01:38,495
Nobody else can take them.

28
00:01:41,138 --> 00:01:44,999
And this is not a mock-up: the same rescue ran on chipnet,

29
00:01:44,999 --> 00:01:49,476
accepted by a real node next to Paryon's unmodified contracts.

30
00:01:50,434 --> 00:01:54,611
Every guarantee is enforced on chain by Bitcoin Cash itself.

31
00:01:54,611 --> 00:01:57,273
No server, no database, no account.

32
00:01:57,273 --> 00:01:58,400
Backstop.
